1
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,800
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:46,000
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:48,320
=Episode 7=

4
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:51,479
We've picked enough vine blossoms.

5
00:00:52,479 --> 00:00:54,399
We're lucky to live in peaceful times.

6
00:00:54,759 --> 00:00:56,759
So we can enjoy days like this.

7
00:00:58,280 --> 00:00:59,039
Look at you.

8
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:01,200
We're here to relax. Why the long face?

9
00:01:01,799 --> 00:01:02,799
Cheer up.

10
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:05,759
I made this herbal sachet earlier today.

11
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,359
The flowers are already inside.

12
00:01:07,799 --> 00:01:09,200
Keep it by your pillow tonight.

13
00:01:09,759 --> 00:01:10,719
You'll sleep well.

14
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:24,760
Does this herbal sachet

15
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:26,959
contain only vine blossoms?

16
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:35,560
No.

17
00:01:40,159 --> 00:01:42,760
And I had a little motive of my own.

18
00:01:43,359 --> 00:01:44,439
Vine blossoms have a cooling effect.

19
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:46,079
Your pulse suggests poor circulation.

20
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:48,879
I suspect your hands
and feet get cold at night.

21
00:01:49,519 --> 00:01:51,719
So I added a few mild herbs.

22
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:53,599
The herbs may look a little dark,

23
00:01:54,079 --> 00:01:56,159
but they're gentler than people.

24
00:01:57,239 --> 00:01:58,760
If you still don't trust me, Mr. Gu,

25
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:00,359
leave the herbal sachet here.

26
00:02:00,799 --> 00:02:02,560
I'll sell it to the next insomniac.

27
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:10,280
What if your herbal sachet works so well

28
00:02:11,519 --> 00:02:12,959
I sleep soundly every night

29
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,599
and can't do without it?

30
00:02:16,879 --> 00:02:18,120
Then I hope, Mr. Gu,

31
00:02:18,759 --> 00:02:19,879
you'll sleep just as well

32
00:02:19,879 --> 00:02:20,879
without the herbal sachet.

33
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,439
Today's consultation fee is

34
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:26,719
50 wen.

35
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:37,039
Call it a thank-you

36
00:02:38,159 --> 00:02:40,039
for showing me this beautiful view.

37
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:41,639
May I ask

38
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:43,000
your name?

39
00:02:43,879 --> 00:02:44,560
Su Cao.

40
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:47,360
Thank you, then.

41
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:48,919
I'll be going.

42
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,199
By the way, Mr. Gu.

43
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:58,120
Come back in two days for a follow-up.

44
00:02:58,759 --> 00:03:00,719
Don't dwell on your worries before bed.

45
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:02,280
If you still can't sleep,

46
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:04,879
think of the peace we enjoy

47
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:07,400
and the beauty of these mountains.

48
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:09,680
I will.

49
00:03:10,479 --> 00:03:11,199
Ms. Su.

50
00:03:20,479 --> 00:03:22,960
(Everyone in the palace
who sees His Majesty)

51
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:24,400
(either fears him)

52
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:26,039
(or reveres him.)

53
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,919
(Only the Empress was different.)

54
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,919
(She'd have His Majesty)

55
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:32,400
(steady her ladder,)

56
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:33,800
(move flowers,)

57
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,080
(and grind ink for her.)

58
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,759
(She'd tease him about his handwriting)

59
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:39,439
(and call him clumsy.)

60
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:42,879
(Yet His Majesty loved it.)

61
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:44,800
(Because with the Empress,)

62
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:46,319
(he wasn't a ruler)

63
00:03:46,639 --> 00:03:47,639
(or the emperor.)

64
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:49,879
(He was just a man)

65
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:52,120
(who wanted to be himself.)

66
00:03:52,919 --> 00:03:53,560
(Your Majesty,)

67
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:57,560
(I'm a better replacement for
the late Empress than Consort Chen.)

68
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,120
(Are you satisfied?)

69
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:07,879
Your Majesty.

70
00:04:14,879 --> 00:04:17,479
I haven't seen you these past two days.

71
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:19,479
Could it be...

72
00:04:19,599 --> 00:04:21,199
I've done something wrong

73
00:04:21,639 --> 00:04:22,800
and made you lose interest in me?

74
00:04:25,079 --> 00:04:26,160
You're overthinking it.

75
00:04:27,399 --> 00:04:28,480
I've just had

76
00:04:29,839 --> 00:04:30,680
too much to do lately.

77
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:32,160
No matter how busy you are,

78
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:34,199
you still need to rest.

79
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:36,319
Your Majesty.

80
00:04:36,959 --> 00:04:38,879
If you keep being so cold to me,

81
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:40,480
you'll hurt my feelings.

82
00:04:47,839 --> 00:04:48,720
Your Majesty.

83
00:04:49,199 --> 00:04:50,720
Do I

84
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:52,399
look pretty today?

85
00:05:02,439 --> 00:05:03,759
Of course you do.

86
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:06,839
Then, Your Majesty...

87
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:08,600
look at me a little longer.

88
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:18,300
Oh!

89
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:19,560
Careful!

90
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:24,480
Mr. Gu.

91
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:26,240
Are you here for your follow-up?

92
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,279
There are quite a few people today.

93
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:30,240
So you may have to wait a little longer.

94
00:05:30,839 --> 00:05:31,920
I'm free today.

95
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:32,879
I'll help.

96
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:34,720
All right.

97
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:36,560
Thank you, Mr. Gu.

98
00:05:37,839 --> 00:05:38,560
This way.

99
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,000
I'll do it.

100
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:41,600
Oh.

101
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:44,519
Mr. Gu.

102
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:45,800
Keep an eye on the fire for me.

103
00:05:47,519 --> 00:05:48,079
A headache.

104
00:05:48,319 --> 00:05:49,079
A migraine?

105
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:49,800
Yes.

106
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:52,560
Mr. Gu.

107
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:00,800
This one?

108
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:01,120
Mm-hmm.

109
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:05,480
Thank you, miss.

110
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:16,759
Mr. Gu.

111
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:23,240
It'll be ready in a moment.

112
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:27,959
Here. This is for you.

113
00:06:29,079 --> 00:06:30,040
Thank you!

114
00:06:57,360 --> 00:07:01,547
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

115
00:07:01,681 --> 00:07:05,294
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

116
00:07:05,529 --> 00:07:08,128
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

117
00:07:08,165 --> 00:07:10,445
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

118
00:07:10,492 --> 00:07:14,321
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

119
00:07:14,723 --> 00:07:18,076
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

120
00:07:19,003 --> 00:07:22,516
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

121
00:07:23,016 --> 00:07:25,583
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

122
00:07:25,709 --> 00:07:27,742
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

123
00:07:27,809 --> 00:07:31,586
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

124
00:07:31,936 --> 00:07:36,269
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

125
00:07:36,492 --> 00:07:39,999
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

126
00:07:40,180 --> 00:07:43,033
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

127
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:48,714
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

128
00:07:48,754 --> 00:07:51,768
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

129
00:07:51,809 --> 00:07:57,817
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

130
00:07:58,484 --> 00:08:05,439
♪The past has faded away♪

131
00:08:05,439 --> 00:08:09,239
♪The past has faded away♪
